1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,788
A wall of logs can hide useful clues.

2
00:00:03,392 --> 00:00:07,281
EZ PM2 GUI turns a snapshot into a focused

3
00:00:07,316 --> 00:00:08,164
conversation.

4
00:00:08,605 --> 00:00:11,983
This walkthrough uses sample logs and simulated analysis.

5
00:00:12,494 --> 00:00:14,201
Connect from the process sidebar.

6
00:00:14,584 --> 00:00:16,767
The list updates when the connection is ready.

7
00:00:17,278 --> 00:00:20,645
Open the service logs, then select Analyze logs to reveal
the

8
00:00:20,691 --> 00:00:22,142
persistent right sidebar.

9
00:00:22,746 --> 00:00:26,415
Expand AI Settings and choose an available provider:
Ollama

10
00:00:26,473 --> 00:00:29,538
local or cloud models, or an installed cloud-connected

11
00:00:29,596 --> 00:00:30,769
command-line provider.

12
00:00:31,373 --> 00:00:34,670
For cloud analysis, review the sharing notice and
explicitly

13
00:00:34,716 --> 00:00:37,143
allow the snapshot and conversation to be sent.

14
00:00:37,584 --> 00:00:40,103
Inspect the redacted snapshot before sending it.

15
00:00:40,614 --> 00:00:42,936
The preview shows captured lines and limits.

16
00:00:43,377 --> 00:00:46,721
Ask a concrete question: why is this service restarting?

17
00:00:47,232 --> 00:00:48,544
Then start the analysis.

18
00:00:48,985 --> 00:00:51,678
The Markdown response appears separately from your
question.

19
00:00:52,189 --> 00:00:55,742
Follow cited lines, distinguish observations from
hypotheses,

20
00:00:55,916 --> 00:00:57,483
and review suggested checks.

21
00:00:57,994 --> 00:01:00,583
Verify the evidence before changing the application.

22
00:01:01,094 --> 00:01:04,217
Choose a suggested follow-up to fill the composer, then
send it

23
00:01:04,241 --> 00:01:04,856
when ready.

24
00:01:05,460 --> 00:01:07,909
Requests and responses are saved in SQLite.

25
00:01:08,513 --> 00:01:11,706
Reopen your conversation from history and continue with
the same

26
00:01:11,752 --> 00:01:12,611
context.
